<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese eleven month car sales up 7.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese eleven month car sales up 7.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto-Dealers Association (ACAP) announced the following new car registrations:</p>
<p>November 1996: 15,806 vs 14,430 (up 9.5 pct)</p>
<p>Jan/Nov  1996: 197,798 vs 184,730 (up 7.1 pct)</p>
<p>First 11 months by manufacturers market share (percentage in brackets). comparative figures refer to same period 1995:</p>
<p>    Fiat	  29,521 (14.92) vs 29,053 (15.73)</p>
<p>    Opel	  28,394 (14.36) vs 28,749 (15.56)</p>
<p>    Renault     25,091 (12.69) vs 23,914 (12.95)</p>
<p>    Ford	  19,555  (9.89) vs 15,685  (8.49)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen  16,129  (8.15) vs 13,807  (7.47)</p>
<p>    Peugeot     12,799  (6.47) vs 13,515  (7.32)</p>
<p>    Citroen     11,972  (6.05) vs  9,655  (5.23)</p>
<p>    Rover	  7,542  (3.81) vs  5,925  (3.21)</p>
<p>    Honda	  6,731  (3.40) vs  6,537  (3.54)</p>
<p>    Seat	   6,416  (3.24) vs  8,366  (4.53)</p>
<p>--Lisbon Bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
